// integration-tests/sample-rejected-lost -- wire types.
//
// A "slow consumer" scenario: a monitoring app that must be correctly
// notified, not silently degraded, when the middleware drops data for two
// different reasons -- reader-side RESOURCE_LIMITS overflow (SAMPLE_REJECTED)
// and writer-side KEEP_LAST history eviction outrunning a reader's ack
// (SAMPLE_LOST). One shared type reused across three topics (RejectedTopic,
// LostTopic, SyncTopic -- the last used only to let the subscriber know the
// publisher has finished writing before it checks final status, avoiding a
// race against exactly how many rejections/losses have landed so far). See
// docs/design/integration-test-tier.md for the full scenario spec.
// Byte-identical copy required in c/, cpp/, java/, zig/.
@final
struct StatusEvent {
    int32 seq;
};
